Add the ``plover_dict_audit`` offline command: it exhaustively checks whether an upgraded plain dictionary stack keeps producing the same text as the old stack for every finite stroke sequence over a user-supplied raw stroke alphabet, within the native English Stenotype pure-text scope (including multi-stroke re-segmentation, prefixes and implicit suffixes, attach/glue, orthography, case and mode, punctuation, word-end, carry capitalization, look-ahead and in-history undo). Out-of-scope branches (plugin metas and macros, retro-case/currency, key combinations, engine commands and undo past the recoverable history) are reported instead of being executed. Incompatibilities come with the shortest counterexample, the first differing stroke or new-side domain exit, and confirmation from an isolated native translator/formatter replay that performs no external operation; resource exhaustion yields an explicit inconclusive verdict.
